WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:04.610
In Lyon, your app opens in
English on a phone set to French.

2
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.530
Its welcome is a plain Text
element that nothing translates.

3
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.320
General Translation lets you translate a

4
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.070
React Native app with
gt-react-native and T.

5
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.310
Add its Babel plugin, which supplies
the polyfills React Native needs.

6
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.890
Call initializeGT with loadTranslations,
then wrap the app in GTProvider,

7
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.930
which reads the device language.

8
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.690
Mark the welcome with T, then
sign in and run npx gt translate.

9
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.170
The package is experimental, and
Expo apps need a development build.

10
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.710
Phones set to Spanish or Japanese show
them, and in Lyon the app opens in French.
